      "html": "<p>Leptodoras myersi Böhlke, 1970. Family Doradidae. Size: 77 mm (3 inches) SL.</p><p>Etymology: Leptodoras comes from the Greek leptos, meaning slender, and doras, meaning skin (also a word commonly used in forming generic names for doradids), in reference to the shape.</p>"
